<title>USA: U.S. chain store sales up 1.0 pct - BTM/Schroders.</title>
<headline>U.S. chain store sales up 1.0 pct - BTM/Schroders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales rose 1.0 percent in the week ended December 7 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were up 2.6 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index was up 0.5 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
